// `break` inside a lambda body inside a `while` (Stage 28 W10b): a
// lambda body is a function of its own, so the loop around it is not one
// its `break` can leave; the checker rejects it ("break is only valid
// inside a loop") on both back ends. Until W10b the checker accepted it
// (its loop depth was not reset for lambda bodies): the old back end
// failed in myc and the new one refused it with L0001 (mir.md W7b.9,
// defect 6). tests/cases/test_frontend.av checks the diagnostic and its
// location. No `fn main`, so the differential leaves it out.

fn run: Int {
  i = 0
  while i < 3 {
    f: fn(): Int = { ||
      break
      1
    }
    i += f()
  }
  i
}
